{
  "dom_id": "step-54190",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Solving for an Unknown Amount",
  "problem": "Amy is baking a loaf of bread. If the loaf weighs $12$ ounces, then Amy needs to bake the loaf for $40$ minutes. There is a proportional relationship between the loaf's weight (in ounces) and the time (in minutes) the loaf needs to bake.\n\nIf Amy leaves the house for $60$ minutes and wants the loaf to be fully baked the moment she returns, how much should the loaf of bread weigh?",
  "worked_solution": "Let $x$ be the loaf's weight (in ounces), and $y$ be the time (in minutes) the loaf needs to bake.\n\nFirst, we need to construct the equation that represents the proportional relationship. Every proportional relationship takes the form $y=kx,$ where $k$ is the constant of proportionality.\n\nWe are told that if the loaf weighs $x=12$ ounces, then Amy needs to bake it for $y=40$ minutes. We can find the constant of proportionality by computing the ratio of the $y$-value to the $x$-value, as follows:\n\n$$\nk = \\dfrac{y}{x} = \\dfrac{40}{12} = \\dfrac{40 \\div 4}{12 \\div 4} = \\dfrac{10}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation is\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{10}{3} x.\n$$\n\nNow, we want to find the value of $x$ so that the loaf will bake for exactly $y=60$ minutes. So, we substitute $y=60$ into the equation above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}60 & =\\frac{10}{3}x \\\\ \\frac{10}{3}x & =60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve for $x,$ we multiply both sides of the equation by the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{10}{3},$ which is $\\dfrac{3}{10}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{10}\\times \\frac{10}{3}x & =\\frac{3}{10}\\times 60 \\\\ 1x & =\\frac{3\\times 60}{10} \\\\ x & =\\frac{180}{10} \\\\ x & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the loaf of bread should weigh $18$ ounces.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-54190\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"54190\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"13100\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-54190\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-8\">Solving for an Unknown Amount</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"54190\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n    